※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4489

※ Joining puts the elements of one array after the elements of another, which
※ is a thing to do to arrays and to nothing else.  A single value is made an
※ array of one by writing it between the array brackets, which is what this
※ program meant and did not say.

let a: u8⟦3⟧ = ⟦1u8, 2u8, 3u8⟧

@[startup]
fn main() → u8:
    let both: u8⟦4⟧ = a ⧺ 7u8
    both⟦0⟧
